    "## Part A — Git Practice\n",
    "\n",
    "Do these in your terminal (Ubuntu, Git Bash, or CMD/PowerShell) — not in this notebook. Screenshot each step for submission.\n",
    "\n",
    "### A1. Terminal basics\n",
    "Create a folder called `lab1-git-practice`, move into it, and confirm you're inside it using the current-path command for your OS.\n",
    "\n",
    "### A2. Full Git workflow\n",
    "Inside `lab1-git-practice`:\n",
    "1. `git init`\n",
    "2. Create a file `notes.txt` with a couple of lines of text.\n",
    "3. `git status` — confirm it shows as **untracked**.\n",
    "4. `git add notes.txt`, then `git status` again — confirm it now shows as staged.\n",
    "5. `git commit -m \"add initial notes\"`\n",
    "6. Edit `notes.txt`, add a new line. Run `git diff` — read the output before doing anything else.\n",
    "7. `git commit -a -m \"update notes\"`\n",
    "8. Run `git log` — identify both commits, their messages, and timestamps.\n",
    "9. Create a `.gitignore` that ignores `*.pdf` and `*.jpg`. Add a dummy `.pdf` file and confirm with `git status` that Git ignores it.\n",
    "10. Rename `notes.txt` to `lab_notes.txt` using `git mv`, then commit the rename.\n",
    "\n",
    "### A3. Mini-project (submission task)\n",
    "1. Create a new project folder `mini-project`, `git init` it.\n",
    "2. Create three files: `readme.txt`, `data.csv`, `report.pdf`.\n",
    "3. Set up a `.gitignore` that ignores `*.pdf`.\n",
    "4. Stage and commit `readme.txt` and `data.csv` in **two separate commits** with meaningful messages.\n",
    "5. Modify `readme.txt`, run `git diff`, then commit the change using `git commit -a -m`.\n",
    "6. Run `git log` and paste the output in your submission.\n",
    "7. Rename `data.csv` to `dataset.csv` using `git mv` and commit the rename.\n"
